WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:05.900
Here's an interesting stitch pattern
that I'm calling Connect the Dots.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.530
It's worked with short rows,

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:13.480
and it isn't hard to knit, but it takes
a bit of planning and concentration.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.340
Let's figure this out
by knitting a single repeat.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.000
Looking at the diagram,

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:25.740
notice that the dot is worked over
nine stitches outlined in red.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.920
It'll be knit using partial knitting,
and these five rows in the diagram

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:35.500
represent a single row
in the knitted piece.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:41.020
The gray boxes in the diagram are
needles that are held out of work.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:48.160
The curved symbols remind us to wrap and
prevent holes when changing directions.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.400
To practice knitting one repeat

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:55.920
of the dots, start by casting
on 19 stitches with the main color.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.640
Knit 6 to 8 rows and end
with the carriage on the right.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.520
Remove the main color
from the carriage and set it aside.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.080
Set your carriage to hold so that any

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:13.080
needles in the D or E
position will not knit.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.960
Opposite the carriage,
pull five needles to hold.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:24.080
Thread the carriage with the contrasting
color and knit across 14 stitches.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.800
Be sure the edge stitches knit
completely and wrap that first needle.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:37.440
Opposite the carriage, put five
needles plus two more in hold.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:45.160
Knit to the right and confirm
all the stitches knit correctly.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.240
Don't forget to wrap.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:58.400
Opposite the carriage again, put two more
needles in hold, knit left, and wrap.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.720
Opposite the carriage one last time,

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:06.640
put two more needles in hold,
knit right, and wrap.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:15.280
This completes the partial
knitting for the dot. Now

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:23.120
put five needles plus two in work
and knit left.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.000
Break the contrasting color yarn
and remove it from the carriage.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.500
Now put all needles in hold position.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.980
With the carriage remaining in hold,

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:43.320
free pass to the right and pick
up the main color yarn.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.700
Now cancel the hold setting.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:51.880
Thread the carriage with the main
yarn and knit eight rows.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.960
You can bind off or just drop
the knitting from the machine.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.840
For an all-over design,

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:05.260
we'll repeat this sequence across the row
and then knit a few main color rows

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:10.520
and repeat the dots again,
alternating the position of the dots.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.800
Have fun knitting your connect
the dots stitch pattern.

